    "reading": {
        "body": "Lambda's infrastructure has experienced security incidents in roughly half of monitored periods over the past three weeks, far more frequently than any other major AI provider.\n\nThe disparity is stark across the twelve providers tracked. Lambda recorded incidents in 62 of 120 observations, while OpenAI reported them in 19 of 126 and Fireworks AI in 15 of 126. The remaining nine providers show single-digit incident counts. Lambda also reached a peak of three concurrent open incidents, double that of OpenAI and Fireworks AI.\n\nFor AI scaling, infrastructure reliability matters because compute capacity depends on it. An AI system cannot deliver consistent performance if the underlying services suffer frequent security events. The frequency of Lambda incidents suggests either more aggressive threat activity against its systems, less effective incident prevention, or more transparent reporting of events. The data does not distinguish between these causes.\n\nThis snapshot covers a three-week window and tracks only disclosed incidents. It does not reveal severity, duration, or whether incidents affected customer workloads or merely internal systems. It also does not explain whether Lambda's higher count reflects the scale of its operations or a genuine reliability gap relative to competitors.",
